## Practice Set 1: Study Buddy Finder

**Program Description:**
A student created a program to help classmates find study partners. The program stores a list of students with their subjects and availability. Users can search for partners by subject and see a list of available students.

**Code Snippets:**
```
// List of students: each entry is a string like "Alex:Math"
students ← ["Alex:Math", "Jordan:Bio", "Taylor:Math", "Casey:Chem"]

// Procedure to find students by subject
PROCEDURE findStudentsBySubject(subject)
{
    matches ← []
    i ← 1
    REPEAT UNTIL (i > LENGTH(students))
    {
        entry ← students[i]
        colonPos ← 1
        REPEAT UNTIL (entry[colonPos] = ":")
        {
            colonPos ← colonPos + 1
        }
        subjStart ← colonPos + 1
        subj ← entry[subjStart..LENGTH(entry)]
        IF (subj = subject)
        {
            APPEND(matches, entry)
        }
        i ← i + 1
    }
    RETURN matches
}

// Example call
mathPartners ← findStudentsBySubject("Math")
```

