## Practice Set 2: Grade Calculator Pro

**Program Description:**
A teacher wants a program to calculate final grades. The program stores a list of assignment scores for each student. It includes a procedure to drop the lowest score before averaging.

**Code Snippets:**
```
// List of scores for one student
scores ← [85, 92, 78, 90, 88]

// Procedure to calculate average after dropping lowest score
PROCEDURE averageAfterDrop(scoreList)
{
    // Find lowest score
    lowest ← scoreList[1]
    i ← 2
    REPEAT UNTIL (i > LENGTH(scoreList))
    {
        IF (scoreList[i] < lowest)
        {
            lowest ← scoreList[i]
        }
        i ← i + 1
    }

    // Sum all scores
    total ← 0
    i ← 1
    REPEAT UNTIL (i > LENGTH(scoreList))
    {
        total ← total + scoreList[i]
        i ← i + 1
    }

    // Subtract lowest and compute average
    avg ← (total - lowest) / (LENGTH(scoreList) - 1)
    RETURN avg
}

// Example call
finalAvg ← averageAfterDrop(scores)
```

